    "narrative": "For June 18, 2026, the engine room of our lineup is driven by **Josh Naylor** (66.36) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (62.80). **Josh Naylor** finds the most favorable path to production tonight against Baz, as his strong platoon advantage against the righty, paired with the +6% boost from occupying the third spot in the order, mitigates the park factor drag. Meanwhile, **Tyler Soderstrom** remains our highest-ceiling bat despite the lineup uncertainty; his elevated park-adjusted base and high-order utility make him a locked-in core piece. **Jose Caballero** also surges into the \"Strong\" tier at 60.11, largely because the projected wind conditions\u2014providing a 10% boost\u2014successfully mask the inefficiencies caused by his negative platoon split against Sean Burke.\n\nOn the bench, **Travis Bazzana** is the most significant exclusion, failing to clear our 40-point \"Zebras Floor\" with a 37.03 score. While his leadoff role usually carries a premium, the combination of facing Drohan and a severe L/L platoon disadvantage crippled his efficiency, forcing a conservative stance to protect our game-day caps. We are also monitoring the lineup status of **Max Muncy** and **Austin Riley**; **Austin Riley** sits at a comfortable 59.69, bolstered by a wind-out scenario and favorable BvP indicators, though we remain vigilant regarding the confirmed defensive alignment.\n\nRisks today are concentrated in our middle infield and the volatility of Baz, who faces both **Cole Young** and **Josh Naylor**. While **Cole Young** provides a subtle 2% boost to his score due to the pitcher's slower delivery\u2014increasing his stolen base potential\u2014the matchup against Baz remains a touchpoint for concern. We are keeping **Corbin Carroll** and **James Wood** in reserve due to team off-days, while **Trevor Story** remains sidelined on the IL. With the rest of our depth including **Mickey Moniak**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Carson Williams**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Kyle Karros**, **Alex Freeland**, and **Henry Bolte** tracking behind today's starters, we are positioned to capitalize on these specific favorable wind and order variables.",
